---
import PlaygroundShell from '../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Simulate it" hint="2,000 restaurants on a 16 km by 16 km city map, crowded in the centre and sparse at the edges. Pick where the user stands, how far to look, and how the index finds candidates.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>Start with <b>Scan every restaurant</b>: all 2,000 distances are computed to find the 855 restaurants within 2 km of the city centre. Switch to <b>Index on latitude only</b>: the index narrows the work to a band 4 km tall, but the band crosses the whole city, so 1,307 restaurants are still checked.</li>
    <li>Choose <b>Own grid cell only</b> with 2 km cells. The user stands exactly on a cell corner, so 221 restaurants are checked but just 200 are found: 655 restaurants inside the circle are missed.</li>
    <li>Choose <b>Own cell plus 8 neighbours</b>: 1,207 checked and all 855 found. Now set <b>Grid cell size</b> to 1 km: just 627 are checked, but 256 are missed, because 3 by 3 cells narrower than the 2 km reach no longer cover the circle.</li>
    <li>Pick <b>Suburb</b> and set <b>Grid cell size</b> to 4 km: own cell plus 8 neighbours now checks 410 restaurants to find 26. A cell size that suits the centre is wrong at the edge, and the other way round.</li>
    <li>Choose <b>Quadtree</b>: it checks 77 for the same 26, because its leaves stay large where restaurants are sparse. Pick <b>City centre</b> again: the same tree checks 1,038 to find 855, reading many small leaves.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg geo" data-geo>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>User stands in
        <select class="pg-in" data-loc>
          <option value="centre" selected>City centre</option>
          <option value="inner">Inner city</option>
          <option value="suburb">Suburb</option>
        </select>
      </label>
      <label>Method
        <select class="pg-in" data-method>
          <option value="scan" selected>Scan every restaurant</option>
          <option value="lat">Index on latitude only</option>
          <option value="cell">Own grid cell only</option>
          <option value="nine">Own cell plus 8 neighbours</option>
          <option value="quad">Quadtree</option>
        </select>
      </label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Search radius <input class="pg-in" type="range" min="0.5" max="4" step="0.5" value="2" data-radius /> <b data-radiusval>2</b> km</label>
      <label>Grid cell size <input class="pg-in" type="range" min="0.5" max="4" step="0.5" value="2" data-cell /> <b data-cellval>2</b> km</label>
      <label>Quadtree leaf holds at most
        <select class="pg-in" data-cap>
          <option value="8">8 per leaf</option>
          <option value="16" selected>16 per leaf</option>
          <option value="32">32 per leaf</option>
          <option value="64">64 per leaf</option>
        </select>
      </label>
      <button class="btn" type="button" data-reset>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-note" data-where></p>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-1)"><h3>Distances checked</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-cand></span><span class="pg-note" data-candnote></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-3)"><h3>Found inside the circle</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-found></span><span class="pg-note" data-foundnote></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-missbox style="--c: var(--role-4)"><h3>Missed (edge problem)</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-missed></span><span class="pg-note" data-missnote></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-2)"><h3>Cells or leaves read</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-cells></span><span class="pg-note" data-cellsnote></span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="geo-mapwrap">
      <svg class="geo-map" viewBox="-0.2 -0.2 16.4 16.4" role="img" data-map>
        <rect x="0" y="0" width="16" height="16" class="geo-bg" />
        <path class="geo-area" data-area />
        <path class="geo-dot" data-dots />
        <path class="geo-ring" data-rings />
        <path class="geo-hit" data-hits />
        <path class="geo-miss" data-misses />
        <circle class="geo-circle" data-circle />
        <path class="geo-me" data-me />
      </svg>
      <ul class="geo-legend pg-note">
        <li><svg viewBox="0 0 10 10" aria-hidden="true"><path class="geo-dot" d="M5 5h0" /></svg> not read</li>
        <li><svg viewBox="0 0 10 10" aria-hidden="true"><circle class="geo-ring" cx="5" cy="5" r="3" /></svg> checked, outside the circle</li>
        <li><svg viewBox="0 0 10 10" aria-hidden="true"><path class="geo-hit" d="M5 5h0" /></svg> checked and found</li>
        <li><svg viewBox="0 0 10 10" aria-hidden="true"><path class="geo-miss" d="M2 2L8 8M8 2L2 8" /></svg> inside the circle but missed</li>
        <li><svg viewBox="0 0 10 10" aria-hidden="true"><rect class="geo-area" x="1" y="1" width="8" height="8" /></svg> cells, leaves or band read</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-out" data-verdict aria-live="polite"></p>
    <p class="pg-note">Model: 2,000 restaurants from one fixed seed on a flat 16 km map, 55% packed around the centre, 30% spread wider and 15% anywhere. The grid starts at the map corner, so the city centre at (8, 8) km sits on a corner for every cell size here. A quadtree square splits into four when it holds more than the leaf limit, down to 10 levels, and a search reads every leaf that touches the circle. Every method then checks the exact distance of each candidate. Distances here are flat; real systems use the haversine formula on latitude and longitude. For scale, a geohash of 5 characters is about 4.9 by 4.9 km and 6 characters about 1.2 by 0.6 km.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  import { query } from '../playground';
  type Method = 'scan' | 'lat' | 'cell' | 'nine' | 'quad';
  interface Pt { x: number; y: number }
  interface Node { x: number; y: number; s: number; pts: Pt[]; kids: Node[] | null; depth: number }
  interface Cfg { loc: string; method: Method; r: number; cell: number; cap: number }

  const SIZE = 16; const N = 2000; const SEED = 42; const MAX_DEPTH = 10;
  const CLUSTER = { share: 0.55, x: 7.6, y: 8.3, sd: 1.3 }; const WIDE = { share: 0.3, x: 8, y: 8, sd: 3.5 };
  const LOCS: Record<string, { name: string; x: number; y: number; note: string }> = {
    centre: { name: 'City centre', x: 8, y: 8, note: 'At (8.0, 8.0) km, exactly on a grid corner: the circle spreads over four cells.' },
    inner: { name: 'Inner city', x: 7.3, y: 8.6, note: 'At (7.3, 8.6) km, inside a cell but not at its middle.' },
    suburb: { name: 'Suburb', x: 13.2, y: 3.4, note: 'At (13.2, 3.4) km, where restaurants are sparse.' },
  };
  const DEFAULTS = { loc: 'centre', method: 'scan', r: '2', cell: '2', cap: '16' };

  function mulberry32(a: number) { return function () { a |= 0; a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) | 0; let t = Math.imul(a ^ (a >>> 15), 1 | a); t = (t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), 61 | t)) ^ t; return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296; }; }
  function makePoints(): Pt[] {
    const r = mulberry32(SEED); const pts: Pt[] = [];
    const gauss = () => { const u = 1 - r(); const v = r(); return Math.sqrt(-2 * Math.log(u)) * Math.cos(2 * Math.PI * v); };
    while (pts.length < N) {
      const k = r(); let x: number; let y: number;
      if (k < CLUSTER.share) { x = CLUSTER.x + gauss() * CLUSTER.sd; y = CLUSTER.y + gauss() * CLUSTER.sd; }
      else if (k < CLUSTER.share + WIDE.share) { x = WIDE.x + gauss() * WIDE.sd; y = WIDE.y + gauss() * WIDE.sd; }
      else { x = r() * SIZE; y = r() * SIZE; }
      if (x < 0 || y < 0 || x >= SIZE || y >= SIZE) continue;
      pts.push({ x: Math.round(x * 1000) / 1000, y: Math.round(y * 1000) / 1000 });
    }
    return pts;
  }
  function buildTree(pts: Pt[], cap: number): Node {
    const root: Node = { x: 0, y: 0, s: SIZE, pts: pts.slice(), kids: null, depth: 0 };
    const split = (n: Node) => {
      if (n.pts.length <= cap || n.depth >= MAX_DEPTH) return;
      const h = n.s / 2;
      n.kids = [0, 1, 2, 3].map((i) => ({ x: n.x + (i & 1) * h, y: n.y + (i >> 1) * h, s: h, pts: [], kids: null, depth: n.depth + 1 }));
      for (const p of n.pts) n.kids[(p.x >= n.x + h ? 1 : 0) + (p.y >= n.y + h ? 2 : 0)].pts.push(p);
      n.pts = []; n.kids.forEach(split);
    };
    split(root); return root;
  }
  function leafCount(n: Node): number { return n.kids ? n.kids.reduce((s, k) => s + leafCount(k), 0) : 1; }
  // Does the circle reach this square? Distance from the centre to the nearest point of the square.
  function touches(n: { x: number; y: number; s: number }, qx: number, qy: number, r: number) {
    const dx = Math.max(n.x - qx, 0, qx - (n.x + n.s)); const dy = Math.max(n.y - qy, 0, qy - (n.y + n.s));
    return dx * dx + dy * dy <= r * r;
  }
  function search(pts: Pt[], trees: Map<number, Node>, c: Cfg) {
    const { x: qx, y: qy } = LOCS[c.loc]; const r = c.r;
    const inside = (p: Pt) => (p.x - qx) ** 2 + (p.y - qy) ** 2 <= r * r;
    let cand: Pt[] = []; const boxes: number[][] = []; let cells = 0;
    if (c.method === 'scan') { cand = pts; boxes.push([0, 0, SIZE, SIZE]); }
    else if (c.method === 'lat') {
      const lo = Math.max(0, qy - r); const hi = Math.min(SIZE, qy + r);
      cand = pts.filter((p) => p.y >= lo && p.y <= hi); boxes.push([0, lo, SIZE, hi - lo]);
    } else if (c.method === 'cell' || c.method === 'nine') {
      const s = c.cell; const cx = Math.floor(qx / s); const cy = Math.floor(qy / s); const d = c.method === 'nine' ? 1 : 0; const keys = new Set<string>();
      for (let i = -d; i <= d; i++) for (let j = -d; j <= d; j++) {
        const X = cx + i; const Y = cy + j;
        if (X < 0 || Y < 0 || X * s >= SIZE || Y * s >= SIZE) continue;
        cells++; keys.add(`${X},${Y}`); boxes.push([X * s, Y * s, Math.min(s, SIZE - X * s), Math.min(s, SIZE - Y * s)]);
      }
      cand = pts.filter((p) => keys.has(`${Math.floor(p.x / s)},${Math.floor(p.y / s)}`));
    } else {
      let tree = trees.get(c.cap); if (!tree) { tree = buildTree(pts, c.cap); trees.set(c.cap, tree); }
      const stack: Node[] = [tree];
      while (stack.length) {
        const n = stack.pop()!;
        if (!touches(n, qx, qy, r)) continue;
        if (n.kids) stack.push(...n.kids); else { cells++; boxes.push([n.x, n.y, n.s, n.s]); cand.push(...n.pts); }
      }
    }
    const candSet = new Set(cand);
    const all = pts.filter(inside); const found = all.filter((p) => candSet.has(p));
    return { qx, qy, cand, candSet, all, found, missed: all.length - found.length, boxes, cells };
  }

  const PTS = makePoints();
  const fmt = (n: number) => n.toLocaleString('en-US');
  const yy = (y: number) => SIZE - y; // north up
  const dotPath = (ps: Pt[]) => ps.map((p) => `M${p.x} ${yy(p.y).toFixed(3)}h0`).join('');
  const ringPath = (ps: Pt[], rr: number) => ps.map((p) => `M${(p.x - rr).toFixed(3)} ${yy(p.y).toFixed(3)}a${rr} ${rr} 0 1 0 ${2 * rr} 0a${rr} ${rr} 0 1 0 ${-2 * rr} 0`).join('');
  const crossPath = (ps: Pt[], k: number) => ps.map((p) => { const x = p.x; const y = yy(p.y); return `M${(x - k).toFixed(3)} ${(y - k).toFixed(3)}l${2 * k} ${2 * k}M${(x + k).toFixed(3)} ${(y - k).toFixed(3)}l${-2 * k} ${2 * k}`; }).join('');

  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-geo]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = query(root);
    const trees = new Map<number, Node>();
    let frame = 0;
    const cfg = (): Cfg => ({
      loc: q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-loc]').value, method: q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-method]').value as Method,
      r: Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-radius]').value), cell: Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-cell]').value), cap: Number(q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-cap]').value),
    });
    function draw() {
      frame = 0; const c = cfg(); const s = search(PTS, trees, c);
      q('[data-radiusval]').textContent = String(c.r); q('[data-cellval]').textContent = String(c.cell);
      q('[data-where]').textContent = LOCS[c.loc].note;
      q('[data-cand]').textContent = fmt(s.cand.length);
      q('[data-candnote]').textContent = `${((100 * s.cand.length) / N).toFixed(1)}% of the ${fmt(N)} restaurants`;
      q('[data-found]').textContent = `${fmt(s.found.length)} of ${fmt(s.all.length)}`;
      q('[data-foundnote]').textContent = `restaurants within ${c.r} km, by exact distance`;
      q('[data-missed]').textContent = fmt(s.missed);
      q('[data-missnote]').textContent = s.missed ? `${((100 * s.missed) / s.all.length).toFixed(1)}% of the answer lies in cells that were never read` : 'none: every restaurant in the circle was read';
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-missbox]').style.setProperty('--c', s.missed ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--role-4)');
      let cellsText = '-'; let cellsNote = 'a full scan reads no cells, it reads everything';
      if (c.method === 'lat') { cellsText = '1 band'; cellsNote = 'one index range on latitude, across the whole map'; }
      else if (c.method === 'cell' || c.method === 'nine') { cellsText = String(s.cells); cellsNote = `grid cells of ${c.cell} by ${c.cell} km${s.cells < (c.method === 'nine' ? 9 : 1) ? ' (some fall off the map)' : ''}`; }
      else if (c.method === 'quad') { const t = trees.get(c.cap)!; cellsText = String(s.cells); cellsNote = `leaves touching the circle, out of ${fmt(leafCount(t))} in the tree`; }
      q('[data-cells]').textContent = cellsText; q('[data-cellsnote]').textContent = cellsNote;
      // map
      const notRead = PTS.filter((p) => !s.candSet.has(p));
      const inside = new Set(s.all);
      const checkedOut = s.cand.filter((p) => !inside.has(p));
      const missed = s.all.filter((p) => !s.candSet.has(p));
      q('[data-area]').setAttribute('d', c.method === 'scan' ? '' : s.boxes.map(([x, y, w, h]) => `M${x} ${yy(y + h)}h${w}v${h}h${-w}z`).join(''));
      q('[data-dots]').setAttribute('d', dotPath(notRead.filter((p) => !inside.has(p))));
      q('[data-rings]').setAttribute('d', ringPath(checkedOut, 0.07));
      q('[data-hits]').setAttribute('d', dotPath(s.found));
      q('[data-misses]').setAttribute('d', crossPath(missed, 0.08));
      const circle = q('[data-circle]'); circle.setAttribute('cx', String(s.qx)); circle.setAttribute('cy', String(yy(s.qy))); circle.setAttribute('r', String(c.r));
      q('[data-me]').setAttribute('d', `M${s.qx - 0.3} ${yy(s.qy)}h0.6M${s.qx} ${yy(s.qy) - 0.3}v0.6`);
      const method = q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-method]').selectedOptions[0].textContent;
      q('[data-map]').setAttribute('aria-label', `Map of ${fmt(N)} restaurants. ${method} from the ${LOCS[c.loc].name.toLowerCase()} with a ${c.r} km circle: ${fmt(s.cand.length)} checked, ${fmt(s.found.length)} found, ${fmt(s.missed)} missed.`);
      // verdict
      const v = q('[data-verdict]'); v.classList.toggle('bad', s.missed > 0);
      const ratio = s.found.length ? (s.cand.length / s.found.length).toFixed(1) : '-';
      let text: string;
      if (s.missed) text = `Wrong answer: ${fmt(s.missed)} of ${fmt(s.all.length)} restaurants within ${c.r} km were never read. ${c.method === 'cell' ? 'Read the neighbouring cells too.' : `Cells of ${c.cell} km are narrower than the ${c.r} km circle, so 3 by 3 cells cannot cover it.`}`;
      else if (c.method === 'scan') text = `Correct, but every search computes all ${fmt(N)} distances, and the cost grows with the city, not with the answer.`;
      else if (c.method === 'lat') text = `Correct, but the latitude range alone returns a strip across the whole map: ${fmt(s.cand.length)} candidates for ${fmt(s.found.length)} results. A one-column index cannot narrow both coordinates at once.`;
      else text = `Correct: ${fmt(s.cand.length)} distances checked for ${fmt(s.found.length)} results, ${ratio} checks per result.`;
      v.textContent = text;
    }
    const schedule = () => { if (!frame) frame = requestAnimationFrame(draw); };
    ['[data-loc]', '[data-method]', '[data-radius]', '[data-cell]', '[data-cap]'].forEach((sel) => { q(sel).addEventListener('input', schedule); q(sel).addEventListener('change', schedule); });
    q('[data-reset]').addEventListener('click', () => {
      q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-loc]').value = DEFAULTS.loc; q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-method]').value = DEFAULTS.method;
      q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-radius]').value = DEFAULTS.r; q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-cell]').value = DEFAULTS.cell; q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-cap]').value = DEFAULTS.cap;
      schedule();
    });
    draw();
  });
</script>
<style is:global>
  .playground .geo-mapwrap { display: grid; gap: 8px 16px; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
  @media (min-width: 640px) { .playground .geo-mapwrap { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 420px) minmax(0, 1fr); align-items: start; } }
  .playground .geo-map { width: 100%; max-width: 420px; height: auto; aspect-ratio: 1; display: block; }
  .playground .geo-bg { fill: var(--surface-2); stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 0.05; }
  .playground .geo-area { fill: color-mix(in srgb, var(--role-2) 14%, transparent); stroke: var(--role-2); stroke-width: 0.05; stroke-dasharray: 0.2 0.12; }
  .playground .geo-dot { stroke: var(--muted); stroke-width: 0.09; stroke-linecap: round; fill: none; opacity: .55; }
  .playground .geo-ring { stroke: var(--role-1); stroke-width: 0.035; fill: none; }
  .playground .geo-hit { stroke: var(--role-3); stroke-width: 0.17; stroke-linecap: round; fill: none; }
  .playground .geo-miss { stroke: var(--bad); stroke-width: 0.05; fill: none; }
  .playground .geo-circle { fill: none; stroke: var(--text); stroke-width: 0.06; }
  .playground .geo-me { stroke: var(--text); stroke-width: 0.1; fill: none; }
  .playground .geo-legend { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 6px; }
  .playground .geo-legend li { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; }
  .playground .geo-legend svg { width: 16px; height: 16px; flex: none; overflow: visible; }
  .playground .geo-legend .geo-dot { stroke-width: 3; }
  .playground .geo-legend .geo-hit { stroke-width: 5; }
  .playground .geo-legend .geo-ring { stroke-width: 1.2; }
  .playground .geo-legend .geo-miss { stroke-width: 1.5; }
  .playground .geo-legend .geo-area { stroke-width: 1; stroke-dasharray: 2 1.5; }
</style>
